  "highlight_scope": "P99 upper-tail ceiling, not full-ROI clipping; SDR64 only has one sampled aperture near the ceiling. Exact saturation EV and absolute DR remain unmeasured.",
  "anomaly": "SDR64 f4.5 and f4 remain about 14-15 percent above the baseline ratio after aperture backtracking. Later stable samples retain the anomaly; causal mechanism not established. Excluded from the four-step 0.63 baseline only, retained in attached data and plotted.",
  "noise_scope": "Three nonconsecutive light frames per aperture are for response/stability; not temporal noise. Eight black frames are used for response offset correction, not an absolute DR result.",
  "prior_round_caveat": "The R2 sixteen-frame measurements use a different scene, exposure range and black-offset handling. Compare ratios and trends, not absolute DN across rounds.",
  "pdr_context": {
    "camera": "Nikon Z9 still-photo RAW",
    "nominal_iso64_point_EV": 11.27,
    "iso100_point_EV": 10.61,
